A structural bottleneck is that cuBLAS writes `out_h` as `[H, N, N]`, while the final layer norm reads across `H` with a huge stride. I’m checking whether `torch.bmm` can write directly into an NHWC-strided output for `B=1`, which would make the final pass coalesced.
